  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Emergency Response for El Ni&#xf1;o Drought Affected Communities in Malawi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the first year, Oxfam and partners will address extreme water shortages and basic survival needs. Critical Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) infrastructure will be rehabilitated, including wells, boreholes, and sanitation facilities, and essential items like soap, buckets, and menstrual hygiene materials distributed. Cash or vouchers will be provided to the most vulnerable and food -insecure households during the lean season. In the second year the focus will be sustaining water treatment and systems, quality monitoring, and hygiene promotion. Throughout both years&apos; protection measures will be implemented to mitigate Sexual and Gender Based Violence (SGBV) risks exacerbated by the drought, including establishing referral services, raising awareness, and training communities on SGBV prevention.</narrative>
  </description>
